<%#
  ONE OF THE PROJECT FOLDER'S DEPTH-ONE SUBFOLDERS, AS A PANEL (2026-09-08, folder panels; spec
  decisions 1, 3 and 6). Until now every subfolder was a <details> section inside the Files panel
  and the whole page shared ONE tiles/list cookie, so a maker could not have their models as tiles
  and their firmware checkout as the Finder browser. A folder is a first-class panel now: the
  page editor can hide it, move it and size it (projects/_panel_slot), and its VIEW is its own, persisted in
  `panels["views"]` under this panel's key.

  Locals: dir (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Dir), key ("folder:<node_id>"), view (one of
  Maker::Project::VIEWS). Reads @project, @page_thumbs, @addon_origins and
  @repo_cards off ProjectsController#show, exactly as the section partial it replaces always did.

  ONLY DEPTH ONE IS A PANEL, AND IT SHOWS ONE FOLDER AT A TIME (2026-11-24, click-through panels;
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-24-project-panel-click-through-design.md §1). In Tiles or List the
  panel shows its own folder, or the one `?at[<panel id>]=<node id>` opened beneath it
  (@panel_paths, ProjectsController#panel_paths): a path bar back up, then the folder's subfolders
  as tiles or rows you open (projects/_folder_tile), then its own files. A repository opened that
  way shows its card first. Nothing beneath the open folder is unrolled — #554's flat sections and
  the closed browser a nested repository used to sit in are gone. The Browser view is unchanged.

  THE FRAME IS `_top`, AND ONLY FOLDER LINKS OPT INTO IT. The section sits in a
  `<turbo-frame target="_top">` (ProjectsHelper#panel_frame_id), so every link inside — a file, the
  Library path, Commits, the file menu — still navigates the page as it did, while a folder tile
  and a path-bar link carry `data-turbo-frame` and advance the URL
  (ProjectsHelper#panel_folder_link_data): only this panel is redrawn, and Back steps out of the
  folder. A view switch replaces the FRAME by its id (ProjectsController#switched_panel_streams).

  THE COUNT IS THE WHOLE SUBTREE, whichever folder is open: the head describes the panel's own
  folder, and a folder of folders must not read "0 files". Tool output counts and draws here like
  any other file (the Files panel's Generated group is gone, 2026-11-19).

  ITS OWN `thumbs filemenu` PAIR. The Files panel wraps its groups in one instance because they
  share a subtree; a panel is a sibling subtree, so a controller mounted over there would not find
  these cells at all. Every tile id here is already in @page_thumbs: ProjectsController#show's union
  takes each shown folder's own files — the open folder of every Tiles or List panel, which is
  exactly what this draws — so this polls, and never builds a second ThumbnailMap.

  THE COUNT ADDS WHAT FILE_CAP LEFT OUT (`subtree_hidden_count`, 2026-11-12), and so does "empty":
  a folder the cap cut reads its real size, never "0 files · Empty folder" over files the scan
  indexed (Maker::ProjectFolderListing's header has the live case). The "Showing X of Y" line is
  for the tiles and the list only, and counts the OPEN folder's own files; the browser lists every
  file, so it needs none.
%>
<% hidden = dir.subtree_hidden_count %>
<% count = (dir.repo? ? dir.subtree_file_count : dir.subtree_file_ids.size) + hidden %>
<% empty = count.zero? && dir.children.empty? %>
<%# THE FRAME'S ID IS DERIVED FROM THE LAYOUT KEY, AND A VIEW SWITCH REPLACES THE FRAME BY IT
    (2026-11-16; the frame since 2026-11-24): the stream ProjectsController#show answers a press
    with targets panel_frame_id(key), and a folder link names the same frame — a colon-free
    spelling, and that helper says why. An id that drifted from the key would leave the buttons
    saving the view and the page not changing, with no error anywhere. The SECTION keeps the key
    itself: anchors land on it, and the editor and the tests name it. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag panel_frame_id(key), target: "_top", class: "panel-frame" do %>
<section class="panel folder-panel<%= " panel--quiet" if empty %>" id="<%= key %>">
  <div class="panel-head">
    <%# THE FOLDER'S OWN NAME IS THE DEFAULT, NOT THE TITLE (2026-09-09, the page editor): only this
        caller knows it — Layout holds node ids and PANEL_LABELS names no folder — so it is passed
        in, and the maker's own title wins over it when there is one. %>
    <h2><%= panel_title(@panel_layout, key, dir.name) %></h2>
    <span class="mono muted"><%= pluralize(count, "file") %></span>
    <%# WHERE IT IS, not just what: the subfolder's path, linked to it in the Library. The Files
        panel's own `panel-path` reads "Open folder →" since slice 6, with the path as its title —
        that folder is the page's own subject, where a subfolder's path is the news. %>
    <%= link_to dir.path, files_path(folder: dir.node_id), class: "panel-path mono muted" %>
    <% if dir.repo? %><span class="badge">repo</span><% end %>
    <div class="panel-actions">
      <% if dir.repo? %>
        <%= link_to "Commits", repo_commit_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn", data: { turbo_prefetch: false } %>
        <%= link_to "History", repo_history_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn", data: { turbo_prefetch: false } %>
      <% end %>
      <%# THIS PANEL'S VIEW BUTTONS, all three of Maker::Project::VIEWS (projects/_view_toggle, which
          says why they are buttons and how a press replaces this panel alone). The Files panel
          renders the same partial and is offered two: it has no browser to mount, because there is
          no Dir for the folder's own root unless it is a working tree, and a control that does
          nothing is worse than one that is absent. %>
      <%= render "projects/view_toggle", key: key, view: view, label: "View of #{dir.name}" %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%= panel_intro(@panel_layout, key) %>
  <%# VERSION STACKS, THIS PANEL'S OWN SWITCH (spec §9): not in the browser, which lists every file. %>
  <% if count > 1 && view != "browser" %>
    <%= render "projects/stack_switch", key: key, label: dir.name %>
  <% end %>

  <% if empty %>
    <%# QUIET, NOT OMITTED (S4-1's quiet-panel rule). The maker put this folder in the layout — it
        is a real folder on disk — so the honest render is its heading and one sentence, the same
        answer an empty Tasks panel gives. Omitting it is the VISITOR's page's rule, not this one. %>
    <p class="muted">Empty folder.</p>
  <% else %>
    <div data-controller="thumbs filemenu stack" data-thumbs-url-value="<%= thumbnails_files_path %>">
      <%# THE CARD COMES FIRST IN EVERY VIEW AND AT EVERY OPEN FOLDER — the README rendered, the
          latest commit, the current tag — and a repository opened beneath it adds its own card
          below the path bar. @repo_cards holds one for every repo? Dir on the page (ProjectsController#show), so a
          missing entry would be a real bug rather than a normal case; the `&&` is defensive. %>
      <% if dir.repo? && (card = @repo_cards[dir.node_id]) %>
        <%= render "projects/repo_card", card: card %>
      <% end %>
      <% if view == "browser" %>
        <%# THE FINDER-STYLE BROWSER (2026-09-07), which takes any Dir — a plain folder switched to
            this view browses exactly as a repository does, and it REPLACES the tiles and the rows
            rather than sitting above them. It opens at the panel's own folder whatever `?at=` says. %>
        <%= render "projects/repo_browser", dir: %>
      <% else %>
        <%# ONE FOLDER AT A TIME (2026-11-24, click-through panels): the panel's own folder, or the
            one `?at=` opened beneath it (@panel_paths), then its subfolders as tiles you open and
            its own files, as figures — a stack stands once where its first member stood, and a
            backup it holds joins it from the Files panel's Backups group
            (ProjectsHelper#stack_figures). A stale `at` never reaches here:
            ProjectsController#panel_paths drops it, and a path the tree cannot resolve falls back. %>
        <% path = (@panel_paths&.fetch(dir.node_id, nil) || [ dir.node_id ]).map { |id| id == dir.node_id ? dir : @listing.dir(id) } %>
        <% path = [ dir ] if path.any?(&:nil?) %>
        <% here = path.last %>
        <% if path.size > 1 %>
          <%= render "projects/folder_path", path: path, key: key %>
          <%# THE OPENED FOLDER'S OWN CARD, when it is a repository of its own. The panel's card above
              is its own folder's and stays at every depth. %>
          <% if here.repo? && (card = @repo_cards[here.node_id]) %>
            <%= render "projects/repo_card", card: card %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
        <% figures = stack_figures(here.files, folder_id: here.node_id) %>
        <% if here.children.empty? && figures.empty? && here.hidden_count.zero? %>
          <p class="muted">Empty folder.</p>
        <% elsif view == "list" %>
          <%= render "file_rows", rows: here.files, figures: figures, folders: here.children,
                     panel_id: dir.node_id, key: key %>
        <% else %>
          <div class="attachments-grid">
            <% here.children.each do |child| %>
              <%= render "projects/folder_tile", dir: child, panel_id: dir.node_id, key: key %>
            <% end %>
            <% figures.each do |figure| %>
              <% if figure.is_a?(ProjectsHelper::StackFigure) %>
                <%= render "projects/stack_tile", figure: figure %>
              <% else %>
                <%= render "file_tile", row: figure %>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <% if here.hidden_count.positive? %>
          <p class="muted attachments-truncated">Showing <%= here.files.size %> of <%= here.files.size + here.hidden_count %> files in this folder. <%= link_to "Open the folder", files_path(folder: here.node_id) %></p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>
<% end %>
